    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0992" n="896" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg896"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.51/363: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-10T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1926—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Your despatch No. 1470 May 17.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d577-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Has the requisite action been taken by the Portuguese authorities? If not,
                        you should remind them courteously of paragraphs 2 and 3 of the Department’s
                        No. 13, May 13, 7 p.m.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>American holdings are unofficially estimated at 12,000 pounds sterling but
                        the number of American bond-holders is not known to the Department.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
